:name: CANable 2.0
:description: CANable 2.0 firmware on an STM32G431 with a simulated USB host exposing the CDC port

# Usage (paths are relative to the repository root, run it from there):
#   renode renode/canable2.resc            (then type `start` in the monitor)
# The CDC virtual COM port is available as a pty, talk SLCAN to it with e.g.
#   picocom /tmp/canable2-cdc               (type V<Enter> with CR line endings)

$name?="canable2"
$bin?=@build/canable2.elf
$pty?="/tmp/canable2-cdc"
# Host SocketCAN interface the simulated bus is bridged to (create with `sudo ip link add dev vcan0 type vcan`)
$can?="vcan0"

using sysbus
mach create $name

include @renode/peripherals/STM32G4_USB.cs
include @renode/peripherals/STM32G4_RCC.cs
include @renode/peripherals/STM32G4_FlashController.cs

machine LoadPlatformDescription @renode/canable2.repl


emulation CreateUartPtyTerminal "cdc" $pty
connector Connect sysbus.usb cdc

# Virtual CAN bus the controller is attached to; other nodes (and the host, via SocketCAN) join it here
emulation CreateCANHub "canHub"
connector Connect sysbus.fdcan1 canHub

# Bridge to the host: frames on the simulated bus appear on $can and vice versa
machine CreateSocketCANBridge "socketcan" $can
connector Connect socketcan canHub

macro reset
"""
    sysbus LoadELF $bin
"""

runMacro $reset
